Rules of grammar are just guidelines to tell you how
the majority of users of the language speak and write, 
so that you can communicate clearly with them.  It's good
to keep the rules in mind, so that when you vary from them,
you are aware that you are deviating from the norm.  
Sometimes it is good to deviate from the norm, because it
makes one's writing and speech interesting and lively.
Other times it is not good, because it makes one ambiguous.


